  "gameRulesSetteEMezzo": "7️⃣ SEVEN AND A HALF\n\n📜 OBJECTIVE\nGet as close as possible to 7.5 points without going over.\n\n🃏 CARD VALUES\n• Cards 1-7: face value\n• Jack, Horse, King: ½ point each\n• King of Coins (Matta): takes any value (0.5 to 7)\n\n⭐ SEVEN AND A HALF REALE\nMaking 7.5 with only 2 cards (a 7 + a face card) beats any other 7.5.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎯 MODE: DEALER VS ALL\n\n📋 GAMEPLAY\n1. One player is the dealer (bank)\n2. Each player places their bet\n3. The dealer distributes cards and plays last\n4. At the end, the dealer decides:\n   • Which players to take from (if beaten)\n   • Which players to pay (if they beat the dealer)\n   • If busted, pays all players\n\n💱 DEALER CHANGE\n• Any player can declare themselves dealer\n• The current dealer must confirm\n• If confirmed, the handover occurs\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🎯 MODE: 1 VS 1 WITH POT\n\n📋 GAMEPLAY\n1. There's a common pot\n2. The dealer plays against one player at a time\n3. There's no fixed order\n4. Each player can:\n   • Pay the dealer an amount (goes into pot)\n   • Request money from dealer (dealer confirms and player takes from pot)\n\n💱 DEALER CHANGE\n• Any player can declare themselves dealer\n• The current dealer must confirm\n• If confirmed, the pot goes to the outgoing dealer\n• The new dealer starts with empty pot",
  "gameRulesCucu": "🐦 CUCÙ (SALTACAVALLO)\n\n📜 OBJECTIVE\nDon't have the lowest card at the end of the turn.\n\n🃏 CARD HIERARCHY\nFrom highest to lowest:\nKing > Horse > Jack > 7 > 6 > 5 > 4 > 3 > 2 > 1 (Ace)\n\n📋 GAMEPLAY\n1. Each player receives one face-down card\n2. Starting from the dealer's left, each player can:\n   - Keep their card (\"I'm good\")\n   - Swap it with the next player\n3. The next player MUST swap, unless they have a King\n4. The dealer can swap with the deck\n5. Whoever has the lowest card loses a life\n\n🛡️ SPECIAL CARDS\n• King: blocks the swap (who has the King says \"Cucù!\")\n• Ace: is the lowest card, always try to swap it\n\n💀 ELIMINATION\nEach player has 3 lives. The one who runs out loses.\nThe last one standing wins!",
  "gameRulesTrentuno": "3️⃣1️⃣ THIRTY-ONE\n\n📜 OBJECTIVE\nGet 31 points or the highest score with cards of the same suit.\n\n🃏 CARD VALUES\n• Ace: 11 points\n• King, Horse, Jack: 10 points each\n• Number cards: face value\n\n📋 GAMEPLAY\n1. Each player receives 3 cards\n2. One card is revealed to start the discards\n3. In turn, each player can:\n   - Draw from the deck or discards\n   - Discard a card\n4. Whoever reaches 31 declares immediately\n5. Whoever thinks they have a good score can \"knock\"\n6. After knocking, each other player has one last turn\n\n🏆 SPECIAL COMBINATIONS\n• 31: three cards of the same suit totaling 31\n• Three of a kind: three cards of the same value (worth 30.5 points)\n\n💀 VARIANT WITH LIVES\nEach player has 3 lives. The lowest score loses a life.",
  "gameRulesLasVegas": "🎰 LAS VEGAS\n\n📜 OBJECTIVE\nGet the highest OR lowest score. The pot is split between these two winners!\n\n🃏 CARDS AND VALUES\n• Italian 40-card deck\n• Number cards: face value (1-7)\n• Face cards (King, Horse, Jack): 10 points each\n• Single Ace: worth 1 point\n• Two or more Aces: worth 11 points each!\n\n👥 PLAYERS\nFrom 2 to 6 players\n\n📋 GAMEPLAY\n\n1️⃣ DEALING\n• Dealer gives 3 face-down cards to each player\n• Places 4 face-down cards in the center\n• Everyone puts a mandatory bet in the pot\n\n2️⃣ BETTING ROUND\nLike Poker, counter-clockwise:\n• Bet: put an amount in the pot\n• Check/Pass: if no one has bet\n• Call: match someone else's bet\n• Raise: bet more\n• Fold: exit the hand\n\n3️⃣ DISCARDING\nAfter each betting round, dealer reveals a center card.\nAll players MUST discard cards of the same value!\n(If a card already out appears, replace it from deck)\n\n4️⃣ REPEAT\nRepeat betting and discarding for all 4 center cards.\n\n🏆 FINALE\nAfter the last round, show cards:\n• Half pot → HIGHEST score\n• Half pot → LOWEST score\n\n⭐ LAS VEGAS!\nIf a player discards ALL their cards, they make \"Las Vegas\" and win the ENTIRE pot!",
  "gameRulesBestia": "🦁 BESTIA\n\n📜 OBJECTIVE\nWin at least one trick to avoid \"going in bestia\".\n\n🃏 CARDS USED\nItalian 40-card deck.\n\n📋 GAMEPLAY\n1. Each player receives 3 cards (or 4-5 in some variants)\n2. A card is revealed to determine trump\n3. Each player decides to participate (\"Knock\") or pass\n4. Tricks are played like in Briscola\n5. Whoever wins no tricks \"goes in bestia\"\n\n🔥 GOING IN BESTIA\nWhoever wins no tricks must pay a penalty:\n• Usually doubles the existing pot\n• Or pays a fixed amount set at the start\n\n🎴 VARIANTS\n• Three Cards: classic fast version\n• Four Cards: more strategy\n• Five Cards: longer games\n• With Accomodo: before playing you can swap cards\n\n💡 STRATEGY\nIf you have weak cards, better to pass than risk going in bestia!",
